{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "0af4d8c5-76dd-87b2-b5aa-a7cdc477d75f",
  "created_at": "2026-02-26T10:53:09-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Celeste Rocha",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:50:06-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:50:10-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Tony. My name is Celeste Rocha. I am calling about my water and sewer bill. It says estimated read, and I think nobody came to read my meter. Not in a long time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:50:22-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, sure. Estimated just means the bill was calculated from your past usage instead of a fresh reading off the meter. Do you have the bill in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:50:33-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I have it here. Sorry, you are on speakerphone, my hands are busy. And on the computer I have forty tabs open, forty, and I cannot find the right one. So I use the paper."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:50:46-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Paper's fine. Look for a line that says consumption, and tell me what it shows."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:50:52-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, consumption. This word, I do not understand well. It is the water that I ate? Sorry, that I used?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:51:00-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Close enough, you used it, yes. Consumption is just the amount of water that went through your meter during the billing period. The charge is based on that number. So when it's estimated, that number is a guess based on your earlier bills."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:51:15-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, okay. So it is not the real water. It is a guess. And I think the guess is too high, because I am only one person in the house most days."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:51:26-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That could be. Estimates can run a little off either way. Can I ask you to read me the dates of the billing period?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:51:35-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It says December first until, um, the end of January. And the amount is one hundred one dollars and twenty-five cents."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:51:43-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. I can put in a request to have the meter read again so we can check it against the estimate. If the real number is lower, the next bill gets adjusted."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:51:55-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please, I would like that. Re-check the read. Because I think nobody opened the little cover outside."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:52:02-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood, I'll note that on the account. Do you want to take care of this bill today too, or wait for the re-read?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:52:11-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, I want to pay now. I do not like to have it waiting. I pay one hundred one twenty-five by card, is okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:52:20-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine, go ahead whenever you're ready with the card number."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:52:25-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I go slowly. Three seven eight two. [pause] Eight two two four six three. [pause] One zero zero zero five. The expiration is zero nine, thirty."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:52:35-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Let me read that back. Three seven eight two, eight two two four six three, one zero zero zero five, expiring oh nine thirty, for one hundred one dollars and twenty-five cents. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:52:48-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that is correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:52:50-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. That's processed. You'll see it on the account, and I've put the re-read request in as well. Someone should be out to the meter in the next couple of weeks."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:53:01-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you very much, Tony. You explained very clear. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-26T10:53:06-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too, Ms. Rocha. Take care."
    }
  ],
